WEBVTT

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.210
Go away.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.880
Go away!

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.500
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.430
That's not... why I'm here.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.980
I just wanted...

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.480
...to apologize to her!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.120
Tears Overwritten

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.370
Oh, God.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.500
I'm a horrible person.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.090
I left Watanabe-<i>san </i>with him.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:37.430
It's my fault Naracchi
was forced to quit JPX.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.260
What do you mean?

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.690
I'm not Ai-<i>chan</i>, but if you want,
I can hear you out.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.400
I mean, I <i>am </i>her room--

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.610
Whoa! No sharing personal information!

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.700
Narata-<i>sensei</i>?! What are you doing here?

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.120
I wasn't going to let the two of you
go by yourselves.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.540
Who knew if this guy was a total perv.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.500
A... total perv?

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.670
He's not a perv, he's a stalker!

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.580
I-It's okay.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.800
Perv, stalker, call me whatever you want.
It's my fault, anyway.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.420
Sorry to bother you.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.140
Please, wait!

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.310
Ai-<i>chan </i>might've told me
that we weren't friends,

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:29.310
but that really sucks, and I still want
to try to be friends with her!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.730
Could you please tell me what happened
between you two, Mister Stalker?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.370
Sarasa Watanabe's with a guy?! No way!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.710
Oh my God, he's so ugly.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.710
But I guess she <i>would </i>be into that.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.210
Here.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.210
Thanks.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.300
Wait, Narata-<i>sensei</i>'s there, too?

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.300
Thank you!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.060
So...

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.690
I used to be an unemployed shut-in
who never left the house.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.770
Wow, Mister Shut-In!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:17.280
I was never good with people,
so I started ditching school...

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.530
I spent every day watching anime,
playing games, and browsing the internet.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.040
I love anime, too! I'm super into
<i>Floor Kings </i>right no--

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.540
C'mon, let him talk.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.580
Sorry!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:35.050
One day, I had this music show on, and...

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.510
What?! Who <i>is </i>this girl?!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:42.640
And why does she try so hard
to never, ever smile?

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.220
It hit me like a truck.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.850
She didn't seem scared, or shy, or lonely.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.730
She reminded me of a fantasy princess,

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.560
or an ice queen singing
about letting things go...

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.690
But then, there was that fateful day.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:02.910
Today, we've brought a bunch of your
favorite local mascots to meet the JPX48!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:02.030
Local Mascot Meet n' Greet

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.160
Which is your favorite, Komomo-<i>chan</i>?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:10.410
Oh, wow, I think I like
Starry Boy the best!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.040
I knew 100% she'd fallen from heaven!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.090
That day, June 23rd, the Naracchi Nation
opened to one and all!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.090
"ANONYMOUS: WELCOME TO
THE NARACCHI NATION"

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.800
"ANONYMOUS: She's kinda cute"

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.920
Like when Commodore Perry came to Japan!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.350
That's when I knew... I knew...

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.430
I wanted to open my borders, too!

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.650
I didn't need to worry about
what others thought of me.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.980
I could just be myself.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.280
A fellow Naracchi stan, I presume?

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.040
I made friends and got a part-time job.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.780
"JPX48 Handshake Event"

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.410
Please line up only after double-checking
the number on your ticket!

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.420
"Ai Narata"

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.880
How can I tell her
how much she means to me...

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.670
...in the brief moment
we'll share together?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.640
I have to thank you. I have to!

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.060
I have to tell you!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.150
I-I...

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.320
Naracchi, I...

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.270
I love you!

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.230
Hey, sir--

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.950
Let go, creep.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.240
It took so long to crawl my way up,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.410
but only a second to fall back
to the pits of despair.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:35.210
That's when I remembered the truth.
I'm just a gross otaku.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:38.210
It's not your fault, Mister Gross Otaku!

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.420
You poor guy! Cheer up,
Mister Gross Otaku!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:44.010
I-It's okay, I'm over it.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.930
But to make up for it,
Naracchi was forced to graduate

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.760
"RIP Naracchi lmao"
"does she hate her fans??" "GJ Naracchi."

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:50.850
without even a special event.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:56.520
And all because I held onto
Naracchi's hand for too long.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:58.020
"Ai Narata EXPELLED from JPX"

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:02.150
But I was just one guy. There wasn't
anything I could do about it.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.740
I knew it might've been selfish of me,

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.570
but I wanted to at least
apologize to her...

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:13.080
But that probably just makes me
even more of a creep to Naracchi, huh?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.080
You don't seem like a bad person.
What's your name?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.330
Mister Creepy Otaku!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.170
Okay, Creepy Otaku Man.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.420
Uh, sure, just call me that.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.220
So I've got good news and bad news.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:31.810
The good news is that Ai
doesn't hate you specifically.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.100
She gets creeped out by every man.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.350
Huh?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.560
What probably happened is she'd been holding
back for the whole handshaking event

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.690
and just happened to break
when it was your turn.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.820
Now for the bad news:

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:49.870
Ai isn't as attached to JPX as you hope.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.830
Unfortunately, I can probably say the same
thing about her and the Kouka Troupe.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.670
At some point, Ai gave up on the world

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.660
"Tear Spray"

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:03.840
and started hiding her emotions.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:09.090
Right now, she's just trying to find a
place where she can relax and feel safe.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:15.890
Dealing with people is annoying
and a waste of my time.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.310
But she has so much potential.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.900
I mean, the first time I saw Ai-<i>chan</i>...

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:25.780
I thought she looked like Alice
stumbling into Wonderland.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.990
"How perfect for Kouka," I thought.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.910
She would be the type of person
to stand and shine

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:32.320
in the center of the Kouka stage.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:41.000
I knew I wanted to stand up
on that stage with her.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.170
Narata-<i>san</i>, where are you going?
It's almost time for dinner.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.340
Watanabe-<i>san</i>'s not back yet.
I'm going to go look for her.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.220
I saw her alone with a guy earlier.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.550
Huh?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.180
I have to go!

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.850
What a great pic.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.190
Now, what should I do with it?

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:10.070
She's not here. Oh, God.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.320
What if he did something to her?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.290
What?

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.920
You're not half bad.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.090
I am a rising Kouka star, after all!

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.600
Well then, can you do <i>this</i>?

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.850
<i>Matrix!</i>

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.320
Like this?!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.400
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.740
You came back! What's up?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:56.990
What the hell?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:57.990
Huh?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.660
I really...

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.460
<i>...hate you!</i>

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.750
You... hate me?

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:24.020
My goodness! I can barely
hear you, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.480
Usually you're far too loud!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.650
Sorry, sir.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:29.900
You need to sing a little
louder, too, Yamada-<i>san</i>!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.610
S-Sorry!

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.360
I'm on a diet right now,
so I don't have the energy...

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.280
Oh? Well, that's good,
but take care of yourself, okay?

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.160
Yes, sir.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.330
Okay, let's split into quartets!

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.960
Yamada-<i>san</i>, Hoshino-<i>san</i>,
Narata-<i>san</i>, and Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.800
Hey, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.970
I don't know why you got so mad at me.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.470
Could you tell me why you got angry?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.940
Uh... Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:12.360
If I tell you, will you finally
leave me alone?

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.110
Huh?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:19.620
I felt horrible for running off
and leaving you there with him.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.660
It took everything I had just to go back.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.120
But I couldn't believe it.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.710
Believe what?

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:33.590
You and Taichi and that guy
were dancing around like <i>idiots</i>!

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.720
Ai-<i>chan</i>,

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.430
that doesn't make sense.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.260
Huh?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.850
If you came back 'cause you were worried
about me, then you should've been happy!

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:49.900
If you were worried, you should've
been glad to see I was okay!

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.690
You're just trying to pick a fight now!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.820
Just don't bother me anymore, okay?

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.450
Fine, then! We're <i>through</i>!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.200
Nothing's through!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.950
I told you, we <i>aren't friends</i>!

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:26.640
I told a girl I wanted to be
friends with that "we're through."

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.520
How dramatic.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:32.940
But I still won't start to hate her.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:37.820
She has so many qualities I admire.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.610
I can't help but look up to her.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:50.000
Don't feel like you have to rush.
You're just getting to know each other.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.090
Just take your time and keep at it.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:57.300
But remember, you might not
get what you want.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:13:02.340
Your feelings may be one-sided in the end,
and you'll have to look on from afar.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.640
But I think that's beautiful
in its own way.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:08.850
One-sided feelings are beautiful...

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.650
Akiya-<i>kun </i>is so poetic sometimes!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:17.230
Dammit, Kouzaburou! Stop tweeting
and pretending to be me!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.820
I figured it would be too heavy
for you to handle, Akiya.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.750
Let her be late.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:41.300
I don't want to go to class.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.890
Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.260
Narata-<i>sensei</i>!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.970
I can't find Ai. Have you seen her?

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:53.440
Oh, I assumed she felt bad
and went back to the dorm.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.190
Is she actually skipping class?

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.110
I hope that's it.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:58.860
It doesn't look like
she went back to the dorm,

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.820
and she's not picking up her phone.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:05.780
Ai's not the type to wander around town,
either, 'cause of how she sticks out.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:09.700
And she wouldn't want to give strangers
any reason to talk to her,

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.710
so she's likely not breaking any rules.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.830
Thanks for your help.
I'll keep looking for her.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:19.960
Um, do you think she might've been feeling
homesick and went back to Tokyo?

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.840
I really doubt that's the case.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.260
Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.760
Could we borrow you for a moment?

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.740
I wish Watanabe-<i>san</i>
would drop out of school.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.780
Whoa, hold up,
isn't that Naracchi from JPX?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.620
Huh?

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:47.990
Yo, it totally is!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.330
Holy shit, she's so hot!

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.790
Where is Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:57.130
Did she run away because
I said we were through?

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.590
No way, she wouldn't.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.550
Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.670
Y-Yeah!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.460
Are you listening?

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.470
This is you, right?

